anything I put my mind to.

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:05.382
- Well you do

00:02:05.382 --> 00:02:06.370
- If God wants it for me.
- You kind of mastered

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.776
everything that you've done.

00:02:07.776 --> 00:02:10.095
- I don't master it all but
I persevere through it all

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:10.938
and it gives me a chance

00:02:10.938 --> 00:02:13.678
to find the next thing to work on.

00:02:13.678 --> 00:02:15.095
So I'm a fighter.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.550
I know how to take 'em as
much as I can give 'em.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.156
I been a business woman all these years.

00:02:21.156 --> 00:02:24.382
I get a lot of joy, like
when we first managed

00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:26.873
Naughty by Nature, just
taking them from A to Z,

00:02:26.873 --> 00:02:28.297
getting them signed,

00:02:28.297 --> 00:02:29.832
helping 'em create their record,

00:02:29.832 --> 00:02:32.546
helping 'em create their
name, their image, all that

00:02:32.546 --> 00:02:34.879
and watching them put out a hit record

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:35.926
that became platinum.

00:02:35.926 --> 00:02:37.067
There's a good feeling in that

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.581
because you know you had something to do

00:02:38.581 --> 00:02:43.097
with helping someone else
become a super success.

00:02:43.097 --> 00:02:47.001
And now they have opportunity,
their family is good,

00:02:47.001 --> 00:02:49.605
they have a career they can run with,

00:02:49.605 --> 00:02:50.712
that feels good.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:54.115
Just like playing some
role that's super difficult

00:02:54.115 --> 00:02:55.375
or so challenging in some way

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.144
where you got to go to
some deep, dark place

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.405
within yourself,

00:02:59.405 --> 00:03:00.947
or you got to give yourself therapy

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.740
to get through your own mess
so you can play this thing,

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.499
and then you see it on screen
and you see that it worked.

00:03:06.499 --> 00:03:07.887
That feeling is amazing.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.812
It's not really about the
accolades that, those will come,

00:03:11.812 --> 00:03:14.428
but the work, when you feel like

00:03:14.428 --> 00:03:15.261
you know that feeling
- Yes.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.170
- When you feel like, I nailed that.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.187
And you go to sleep that
night feeling like, "Wow!"

00:03:20.187 --> 00:03:21.463
- 'Cause you are in the forefront, honey.

00:03:21.463 --> 00:03:23.353
(chuckles)

00:03:23.353 --> 00:03:24.410
- Well, I don't know.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.830
I don't know what kind of leader I am,

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.928
but I don't know I'm not
trying to be a leader.

00:03:28.928 --> 00:03:30.069
I'm just trying to be me.

00:03:30.069 --> 00:03:32.597
And if something that I
say helps someone else out

00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:34.557
then that's fine, but to go out and say,

00:03:34.557 --> 00:03:37.447
"Okay, I'm the role model
around these here parts

00:03:37.447 --> 00:03:40.337
"and I'm the spokesperson for all women."

00:03:40.337 --> 00:03:42.865
I'm not trying to do that
because we are individuals

00:03:42.865 --> 00:03:45.271
and we all have minds of our owns

00:03:45.271 --> 00:03:47.102
and things we want to say for ourselves

00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:49.498
and I just say the things I
want to say, is what I say.

00:03:49.498 --> 00:03:52.841
Not what other people want me to say.

00:03:52.841 --> 00:03:54.182
I have real people around me.

00:03:54.182 --> 00:03:56.679
I think that's the best way
to maintain your realness

00:03:56.679 --> 00:03:58.638
is to have honest people around you

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.308
who actually care about you.

00:04:00.308 --> 00:04:01.817
So there's a balance.

00:04:01.817 --> 00:04:04.398
I think as creative
people, we can be sensitive

00:04:04.398 --> 00:04:06.865
so there's a way (giggles)

00:04:06.865 --> 00:04:07.698
to talk to us

00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:10.102
but at the same time,
I think it's important

00:04:10.102 --> 00:04:13.978
to really have an idea of where you are,

00:04:13.978 --> 00:04:16.098
who you are

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:18.179
and not have just a bunch
of yes-men around you,

00:04:18.179 --> 00:04:19.152
unless that's your thing.

00:04:19.152 --> 00:04:20.445
Maybe that works for some people,

00:04:20.445 --> 00:04:22.552
but that doesn't really work for me.

00:04:22.552 --> 00:04:23.719
I need to have

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:30.105
realness around me to kind
of break through all the

00:04:30.105 --> 00:04:31.089
smoke and mirrors, if you will.

00:04:31.089 --> 00:04:34.143
And we create a lot here.

00:04:34.143 --> 00:04:37.160
We build this construct around us here,

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.809
so we need to have real people

00:04:39.809 --> 00:04:41.892
to kind of let us know, keep us grounded.

00:04:41.892 --> 00:04:43.603
Keep me grounded, for sure.

00:04:43.603 --> 00:04:46.211
I've always been the kind to
switch for different things.

00:04:46.211 --> 00:04:48.171
I'm interested in different things, too.

00:04:48.171 --> 00:04:51.132
So I have to have the freedom
to step into those worlds

00:04:51.132 --> 00:04:53.252
and not feel like, oh I got to stay here,

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:56.868
keep this certain persona,
be this person, no.

00:04:56.868 --> 00:04:59.653
If I want to go visit Thailand, I'm going.

00:04:59.653 --> 00:05:00.486
You know what I mean?

00:05:00.486 --> 00:05:03.085
And eat some crazy food
that would never eat, maybe.

00:05:03.085 --> 00:05:04.397
Well, I want to try it.

00:05:04.397 --> 00:05:05.230
You know what I mean?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.631
So that's just who I am.

00:05:06.631 --> 00:05:09.645
So I think being okay
with that has allowed me

00:05:09.645 --> 00:05:12.887
to not be afraid to go into
different things and places

00:05:12.887 --> 00:05:14.097
and try different things

00:05:14.097 --> 00:05:17.842
and kind of move my own personal needle

00:05:17.842 --> 00:05:18.839
forward a little bit.

00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:19.727
- [Interviewer] Has
there never been a point

00:05:19.727 --> 00:05:23.151
where you have felt frustration,
sort of, in Hollywood?

00:05:23.151 --> 00:05:23.984
I'm sure maybe it was

00:05:23.984 --> 00:05:25.320
earlier in your career.
- Absolutely,

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.153
absolutely, but you know what?

00:05:26.153 --> 00:05:29.475
You run into stupid people
everywhere, unfortunately.

00:05:29.475 --> 00:05:31.065
Doesn't matter if it's the cab driver

00:05:31.065 --> 00:05:32.620
who doesn't want to stop for you

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:35.678
or go past 110th Street

00:05:35.678 --> 00:05:39.948
or if it's some executive

00:05:39.948 --> 00:05:43.875
who someone managed to
become in a position of power

00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:47.031
to greenlight movies who has no clue.

00:05:47.031 --> 00:05:50.021
I mean, some things are just timing

00:05:50.021 --> 00:05:52.992
and determination and perseverance.

00:05:52.992 --> 00:05:55.948
If you don't have a sense
of your feet on the ground,

00:05:55.948 --> 00:05:58.146
if you're not level-headed to some degree,

00:05:58.146 --> 00:05:59.166
you could really lose it.

00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:02.600
'Cause you literally have
all these people telling you

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.801
how incredible you are,

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.000
and if you don't have a sense

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.465
of yeah, but, I still have
to take out the garbage.

00:06:09.465 --> 00:06:10.843
Do you know what I mean?
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:06:10.843 --> 00:06:12.957
- I still got to walk my
dog and poop up scoop,

00:06:12.957 --> 00:06:13.790
do you know what I'm saying?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:14.623
Scoop up poop.

00:06:14.623 --> 00:06:17.169
If you don't keep your head,

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:20.435
then you could kind of
get a little souped up,

00:06:20.435 --> 00:06:22.849
a little conceited and lose your edge.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:25.405
Or some people take themselves
too seriously after that.

00:06:25.405 --> 00:06:29.533
They feel they have to
do every incredible,

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:31.241
I did Scary Movie 2

00:06:31.241 --> 00:06:32.306
after that.
- [Interviewer] I loved that.

00:06:32.306 --> 00:06:33.454
- It was just because the kids loved it

00:06:33.454 --> 00:06:36.507
and I'm like, I asked
one of my friend's kids,

00:06:36.507 --> 00:06:37.799
"Did you like Scary Movie?"

00:06:37.799 --> 00:06:38.632
And he was like, "Yeah."

00:06:38.632 --> 00:06:40.994
I'm like, "Do you think I
should do Scary Movie 2?"

00:06:40.994 --> 00:06:42.507
He was like, "Yeah."

00:06:42.507 --> 00:06:44.282
Well I trust a nine-year-old, why?

00:06:44.282 --> 00:06:45.740
Because I don't owe them money,

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.187
they don't owe me money,

00:06:47.187 --> 00:06:48.489
they're not gettin' a cut off of it.

00:06:48.489 --> 00:06:50.202
They just, it's just real.

00:06:50.202 --> 00:06:52.429
So I did it, just for fun,

00:06:52.429 --> 00:06:54.067
and then did more critical kind of things

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:55.688
but I mix it up.

00:06:55.688 --> 00:06:57.064
What I don't think we should do

00:06:57.064 --> 00:07:00.692
is limit ourselves in
any way, shape or form

00:07:00.692 --> 00:07:03.738
in terms of what we
think we're capable of.

00:07:03.738 --> 00:07:05.646
And I think that's been
part of the problem.

00:07:05.646 --> 00:07:08.411
We're relegated into
these particular fields

00:07:08.411 --> 00:07:11.226
and who says that you
can only do those things?

00:07:11.226 --> 00:07:13.702
Unless it's something
physically preventing you

00:07:13.702 --> 00:07:15.134
from doing it,

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.565
in which case, leave it alone.

00:07:16.565 --> 00:07:18.318
But other than that,

00:07:18.318 --> 00:07:19.906
go for it, like go for it.

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:22.011
But just be prepared for what

00:07:22.011 --> 00:07:24.378
you are going to deal with those things.

00:07:24.378 --> 00:07:26.519
And when you find people
you can connect to,

00:07:26.519 --> 00:07:27.499
who will support you,

00:07:27.499 --> 00:07:29.498
whether they're male or female,

00:07:29.498 --> 00:07:31.214
those are the people you
need to keep in your life,

00:07:31.214 --> 00:07:32.972
because my partner, Shakim,

00:07:32.972 --> 00:07:35.908
has respected my brain
from the very beginning.

00:07:35.908 --> 00:07:38.808
Not just my get-down,
not just my rap skills

00:07:38.808 --> 00:07:40.476
or not just how cool I am,

00:07:40.476 --> 00:07:43.538
but really, he respected
my mind from the beginning.

00:07:43.538 --> 00:07:46.349
And so, he and I can get
together intellectually

00:07:46.349 --> 00:07:47.616
and come up with something,

00:07:47.616 --> 00:07:49.369
and then we talk shit to each other

00:07:49.369 --> 00:07:50.836
and like, "Yo, I betcha we can.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:51.669
"We can do that.

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:52.502
"You can't do that.

00:07:52.502 --> 00:07:53.479
"Yes we, well that's how we,"

00:07:53.479 --> 00:07:57.190
and then, we bang about
how we can make it happen.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.511
But if he didn't respect me,

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:00.858
then it wouldn't even go there.

00:08:00.858 --> 00:08:03.224
If I didn't respect him,
then it wouldn't go there.

00:08:03.224 --> 00:08:07.265
So, I don't think we always
have to live on an island,

00:08:07.265 --> 00:08:09.086
not with guys or not with women.

00:08:09.086 --> 00:08:11.164
I think we just need
to connect with people

00:08:11.164 --> 00:08:12.794
who get what we trying to go,

00:08:12.794 --> 00:08:14.100
we moving in the same direction.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.403
And the rest, those are the ones,

00:08:15.403 --> 00:08:17.819
the haters or those who
tell you, "You can't do it,"

00:08:17.819 --> 00:08:19.787
the negative ones or the hanger's-on,

00:08:19.787 --> 00:08:21.978
that's the dead weight you got to cut.

00:08:21.978 --> 00:08:24.670
I've had a guy who drove
me in his limousine,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:28.059
tell me his 12-year-old
daughter has a beautiful voice

00:08:28.059 --> 00:08:30.217
and she was afraid to
sing and she would cry

00:08:30.217 --> 00:08:32.214
because her classmates would tease her

00:08:32.214 --> 00:08:34.086
and tell her she's never going to make it,

00:08:34.086 --> 00:08:36.616
she can't do this, and by looking at me,

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:38.047
she started singing again.

00:08:38.047 --> 00:08:40.623
And she's like, "If Queen
Latifah can do it, I can do it,"

00:08:40.623 --> 00:08:42.458
because she looked more like me

00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:45.232
and because she had a
Queen Latifah to look at

00:08:45.232 --> 00:08:47.930
and inspire her to stay on her path,

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.362
follow her dreams.

00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:51.411
So, I think it's been a great thing.

00:08:51.411 --> 00:08:53.108
I feel good about how I've been able

00:08:53.108 --> 00:08:55.014
to impact people's lives.

00:08:55.014 --> 00:08:56.726
